* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Checksum-bound content must be byte-identical in every working tree.
#
# These paths are hashed with sha256 and compared against values committed in
# evidence indexes, dataset manifests, and run manifests. Under the `* text=auto`
# rule above, a checkout on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF, the bytes change, and
# the recorded checksum no longer matches. That makes
# `tests/contract/test_r4_evidence.py` and `tests/contract/test_prompt6_evidence.py`
# fail on any fresh Windows clone while passing in Linux CI, and it makes a
# regenerated evidence bundle record a `dependency_lock_hash` that no other
# platform can reproduce.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions, so the working
# tree stays byte-identical to the committed blob. These rules come last so
# they override `* text=auto`.

artifacts/evidence/** -text
schemas/** -text
tests/fixtures/** -text
uv.lock -text
web/package-lock.json -text
